sVWe do not knowingly collect personal information from an individual under age 16.
p29
I1
sVWhen you participate in our community engagement panel provided in association with Alida, We may receive information about You to assist us with reviewing and responding to any feedback or comments You provide.
p30
I1
sVWhen You enter contests or respond to promotions, We may collect identifiers and commercial information included in Your entry information such as name, email address, physical address, phone number, age, photo, videos, social account information and any other information You provide.
p31
I1
sVWe may receive personal information about You from Greenhouse as described in Section III(B) below.
p32
I1
sVThis information may be used to, among other things, analyze and track data, determine the popularity of certain content, and better understand Your online activity.
p33
I1
sVWe may seek consent to use and disclose Your personal information after it has been collected in those cases where We wish to use the information for a new or different purpose where You have not already consented to such a use of Your personal information.
p34
I1
sVIf We become involved in a merger, acquisition, sale of assets, joint venture, securities offering, bankruptcy, reorganization, liquidation, dissolution, or other transaction or if the ownership of all or substantially all of our business otherwise changes, We may transfer Your information to a third party or parties in connection therewith.
p35
I1
sVFoursquare may collect and use information that identifies you, such as your device type, advertising identifier on your device and device usage information (for example, a date/time stamp and your location when the Service communicates with Foursquare).
p36
I1
sVIf You connect with Twitter through the Service, We receive Your Twitter identity (which includes Your Twitter avatar and user name and Your followers\u2019 user names).
p37
I1
sVWhen calling us, Your telephone number and name may be collected.
p38
I1
sVWe may also receive information about You from our partners, such as their CRM data about You or transaction information collected at the point of purchase.
p39
I1
sVSection 1798.83 of the California Civil Code permits California residents to request from a business, with whom the California resident has an established business relationship, certain information about the types of personal information the business has shared with third parties for those third parties\u2019 direct marketing purposes and the names and addresses of the third parties with whom the business has shared such information during the immediately preceding calendar year.
p40
I1
sVConsequently, if You choose not provide Us with the required personal information, we may not be able to offer You the Service.
p41
I1
sVWe may receive Your location information when You enter or are near one of our partners\u2019 stores such as Your device\u2019s GPS, Bluetooth, NFC or other communications signal and information about nearby WiFi networks, cell towers, and other communications infrastructure.
p42
I1
sVWhere obliged or permitted to disclose information without consent, We will not disclose more information than is required.
p43
I1
sVWe may receive information about You from other digital advertising companies with which We work (\u201cAdvertising Partners\u201d) to help Us deliver ads to You and recognize You across browsers and devices.
p44
I1
sVWe may collect information including identifiers, geolocation, and commercial information about You from third party sources including, but not limited to, social media companies, advertising partners, measurement partners, third party websites, retailers, CPGs, and food service companies, and our employment services provider(s).
p45
I1
sVWe may automatically collect identifiers, commercial information, audio, electronic, visual, or other similar information, geolocation information, internet or other electronic network activity information, and inferences drawn from all of the above, regarding each user of our Service, including: Your location, Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, NFC (near field communication) or other connection information, network connection information, Internet Protocol (IP) address, telephone number, browser and device information, advertising identifiers, the domain name of Your Internet search provider, the Service features You use, and the time of Your use.
p46
I1
sVFlipp may provide an encrypted version of Your information to its advertising partner LiveRamp, to enable better targeted advertising where LiveRamp already possesses Your email address, device ID, or other advertising ID.
p47
I1
sVWe also may share users\u2019 personal information with advertisers for their direct marketing and promotional purposes and so they can provide services to You.
p48
I1
sVWhen You add a loyalty card to your account, redeem a coupon or otherwise interact with a company with which You have a loyalty account, We may collect commercial information and identifiers including Your Loyalty ID and/or Loyalty account number.
p49
I1
sVOur service providers Braze and Appsflyer collect information about Your device when You use the Service, including Your location, account information (including your e-mail address) and device identifier, in order to assist us with providing You with relevant notifications and provide us with analytics to improve our service.
p50
I1
sVWhen You apply for a job through the Service, We may collect identifiers, education information, and professional or employment-related information including: Your name, email address, telephone number, current employer, social media account links, and any information You provide through Your responses to questions posed or in Your cover letter, resume or otherwise through the Careers/Job Openings section of the Flipp.com Website.
p51
I1
sVWe may collect identifiers from You when You register for and use the Service, contact or interact with us, fill out a form, and voluntarily provide Us with Your comments and other content in connection with using the Service.
p52
I1
sVIt should be noted that in certain circumstances, the Service can only be offered if you provide Us with Your personal information.
p53
I1
sVWe may share Your information with advertisers and their service providers who use our services, including but not limited when You read and interact with an advertiser\u2019s flyer, advertising, coupons or rebates, when You enter or are near an advertiser\u2019s physical location, when You make purchases at an advertiser, and when You use a loyalty or reward program of an advertiser.
p54
I1
sVSpecifically, We may disclose information about You to third parties without Your consent where We believe that such disclosure is necessary to determine whether to proceed with a prospective business transaction or to complete a transaction in progress, or where the information is necessary to carry on the activity that was the object of the transaction.
p55
I1
sVInformation may be disclosed to third parties in accordance with our Privacy Policy, including our service providers and business partners, employment service providers, partners, media companies, and advertising partners.
p56
I1
sVAll such information is used by Foursquare for its own purposes in accordance with Foursquare\u2019s privacy policy (available at https://foursquare.com/legal/privacy), as updated from time to time.
p57
I1
sVWe may share your information with affiliate program networks including Amazon, eBay, Impact, and Commission Junction, and the advertisers using such networks, when you interact with content provided through those networks on the Service.
p58
I1
sVWe may share Your information with our marketing automation service providers, such as HubSpot, when You interact with the Service.
p59
I1
sVWe currently use location information in connection with our Apps.
p60
I1
sVWhen You submit a \u201cContact Us\u201d form, We collect identifiers including Your name, phone number, email address, and any other information You choose to provide to Us.
